Path-compressed union-find. Each node points to a parent; union joins two roots; find compresses paths.

```python
class UF:
    def __init__(self):
        self.p = {}
    def find(self, x):
        if x not in self.p:
            self.p[x] = x
        while self.p[x] != x:
            self.p[x] = self.p[self.p[x]]
            x = self.p[x]
        return x
    def union(self, a, b):
        ra, rb = self.find(a), self.find(b)
        if ra != rb:
            self.p[ra] = rb
